  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong multimodal baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_002 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) combines the most promising design choices: multiprofile for richer cell-level information, scgpt as a well-established pretrained RNA encoder, resnet50 as a solid yet relatively fast image backbone, avgpool for efficient multiprofile aggregation, and weighted fusion as a standard multimodal combination strategy. This tests the core hypothesis that combining RNA and image modalities with a strong encoder pair yields high validation accuracy. It is cost-moderate (resnet50 + avgpool is cheaper than imagenet_vit_l + transformer, but more expensive than single-modality baselines), making it an efficient first probe. The resulting accuracy will serve as the reference point for later ablations (e.g., swapping to imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, scvi_n200, or singleprofile) in the remaining 9 experiments."
}

